"The Elder's Croak is an old Artonan story set before cities but not before magic."
"It takes place in a village in the deepest forest of the Mother Planet, with twin wizard brothers."
"The younger had vast authority but was selfish; his name is not remembered."
"The elder had weaker authority but patience, and learned to change his voice with it."
"With a terrible croak he killed the silent unclimbing beasts the jealous younger brother lured."
"The younger devised a spell giving a sound to many, kept only while the giver never makes it again."
"The elder gave away every sound but the croak, and would not even speak his born language."
"His croak grew so mastered that it slew every beast within a week's walk and spared the innocent."
"It ends: 'He lives with a splinter so that we have everything else.'"
"Listeners traditionally try to croak the name themselves; it must not be rushed on first hearing."
"Tellers vary it; the common version has the elder pleading and praising the younger into helping."
